The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's
real, compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — where the
landed sibling battery P7 pages (BatteryCells, BatteryDegradation; both ledger status=done)
ship, and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path. Page hosting uses the
proven `*RouteRegistration` pattern. The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Battery/**` — the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Battery`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only
deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9. It is identical
to the reconciliation used by the landed sibling p4-apple P7 battery pages.

Manifest "Data sources — (no API data sources)" vs the actual web source: the web page DOES
fetch `GET /analytics/range-projection?vehicle_id` via `useQuery(['range-projection', id])`
and renders 4 data states (PageContainer loading / error + the `!data` empty + per-section
EmptyStates). To honor the manifest's explicit `loading · empty · error · success` requirement
AND the actual web behaviour, the page binds an injectable `ProjectedRangeDataSource` seam
(production → KMP repositories, ADR-004; previews/tests → doubles) that resolves all four
phases — never narrower than the web source.

