================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI ProjectedRangePage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success
over an injectable ProjectedRangeDataSource seam whose ProjectedRangeData value type mirrors the
KMP /analytics/range-projection wire shape 1:1. The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle/VehicleSelect), the five hero MetricCards (Your/Tesla estimate, Battery, Usable
Capacity, Health Factor), the efficiency RadialGauge + accuracy note, the rated-vs-projected
AreaChart with the current-battery reference, the range-scenario cards (icon + current ring +
condition chips + extras), the personal efficiency-matrix heatmap (temp×speed Grid with band tints
and "—" gaps), the what-if calculator (two TSSliders + interpolated range/efficiency/conditions),
the range-factor cards (signed-% impact badges), and the range tips — all from the P2 tokens + P3
shared components (no hand-rolled glass, no direct Charts/recharts). Every data source implements
loading/empty/error/success and every section its own empty state; every visible string resolves
from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (27 manifest + 6 supporting keys added); SI
kilometres/watt-hours convert only at the render boundary via the shared Units facade (ADR-005);
adaptive macOS/iPad vs iPhone-compact layout (ADR-002/006); a11y labels/traits + Dynamic Type +
light/dark honored. Two type-name collisions with PRE-EXISTING module surfaces were resolved by
renaming MY types (RangeProjection→ProjectedRangeData vs the date-range-picker; ProjectedRangeFormat
→ProjectedRangePageFormat vs the ProjectedRangeWidget) — never by touching the incumbents.
Verified GREEN: xcodegen (0), swiftformat --lint (0/14), swiftlint --strict (0/14), placeholder gate
(0), the FULL app target BUILD SUCCEEDED on BOTH macOS and iOS-Simulator with only the one
